<title>USA: Central Garden to acquire Sandoz Agro Inc.</title>
<headline>Central Garden to acquire Sandoz Agro Inc.</headline>
<dateline>LAFAYETTE, California 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Central Garden &amp; Pet Co said Monday it had entered into a definitive asset purchase agreement to acquire Sandoz Agro Inc's flea and tick business in the U.S. and Canada for $41 million.</p>
<p>The company said it expected the acquisition to close before March 1997, depending upon the approval of the merger of Sandoz Ltd and Ciba-Geigy Ltd into Novartis Inc.</p>
<p>The acquisition includes ownership in the United States and Canada of the Zodiac and Vet-Kem trademarks as well as those for Ovitrol, Siphotrol, Fleatrol, vIGRen, Petcor, Precor and Natural Signature, it said.</p>
<p>Central Garden &amp; Pet Co distributes lawn, garden and pet products.</p>
</text>
